course: dictionary
lesson: 6015
title: Words for medicine and jokes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Medicinal describes something used to treat an illness or to help the body heal. Medicine is the thing that makes you better, and medicinal tells you that something works like medicine. «Medicinal plants» are plants that people use to help them get well.
explain: Clues help you here. If the sentence is about plants, herbs or cures, medicinal probably means healing. If the sentence is a joke, it may mean something else. Ask yourself what the topic is, then put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Scientists use this word when they study plants. In 2024 scientists in Sumatra reported that an orangutan called Rakus chewed a medicinal plant and spread the juice on a wound on his face. It was the first wild animal seen treating a wound this way, so the plant was helping him heal.
explain: The word can also be a joke. If someone says «a medicinal chocolate», they are pretending the chocolate is good for them, when really they just enjoy eating it. The clue is that the speaker is teasing, not talking about real health.
fact: Medicinal means used to treat illness or helping the body heal.
fact: «Medicinal plants» are plants that people use to treat illness.
fact: «Medicinal properties» are qualities that can help the body heal.
fact: «Medicinal herbs» and «medicinal purposes» are phrases you will see in science and history.
fact: In a joke, «a medicinal chocolate» is something you enjoy but pretend is good for you.
exercise: «The scientists studied a medicinal plant in the forest.» What does medicinal mean here? | Found only in shops | A plant that grows only in the sea | Very tall and green | *Used to help the body heal
exercise: «Rakus chewed a medicinal plant and spread the juice on a wound.» What was the plant used for? | *To help a wound heal | To make a loud noise | To build a nest | To make a fruit salad
exercise: Dad says, «This chocolate is medicinal, it's so good for you!» Why is Dad joking? | He is talking about a cure for a cold | Chocolate is always real medicine | He is a doctor giving real medicine | *He is pretending the chocolate is good for you because he enjoys it
test: What does medicinal mean in «medicinal herbs»? | *Herbs used to treat illness | Herbs that grow in gardens | Herbs that are sold only in shops | Herbs that smell nice
test: Which sentence uses medicinal as a joke? | «The medicinal plant grew by the river.» | *«This medicinal cake is my favourite treat, honest, it's good for me!» | «Scientists studied medicinal herbs in the lab.» | «The doctor gave me medicinal tablets.»
exam: Which word best matches the meaning of medicinal? | Loud | Poisonous | Sweet | *Healing
